@startuml leader-follower-failover-sequence
title Alert Evaluator — Leader-Scoped Candidate Consumption (Pre-CP2A)

skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #888888
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #CCCCCC
skinparam sequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor #FAFAFA

participant "Instance A" as A #DBEAFE
participant "Instance B" as B #D1FAE5
participant "Redis\n(alert-evaluator:leader)" as Redis #FEF9C3
participant "Kafka\nalert-evaluator group" as Kafka #FCE7F3

== Startup — A acquires the lease first ==

A -> Redis : SET alert-evaluator:leader A NX PX 15000
Redis --> A : OK
A -> Kafka : startCandidateConsumerSession()\nconnect + subscribe + run
Kafka --> A : joined (sole member)
note right of A
  ADR-005: only the perceived lease
  holder intentionally joins/polls the
  candidate consumer group.
end note

B -> Redis : SET alert-evaluator:leader B NX PX 15000
Redis --> B : null (key exists)
note right of B
  running as follower — waiting for
  leader lease. B never calls
  startCandidateConsumerSession().
end note

== Steady state ==

Kafka -> A : proximity.candidates message
A -> A : handleProximityCandidate(...)

== A loses the lease (SIGTERM) ==

A -> A : shutdown()\nabort scan loop
A -> Kafka : session.stop() -> consumer.disconnect()
Kafka --> A : left group
A -> Redis : Lua release (ownership-checked DEL)
Redis --> A : released

== B takes over ==

B -> Redis : SET alert-evaluator:leader B NX PX 15000
Redis --> B : OK
B -> Kafka : startCandidateConsumerSession()
Kafka --> B : joined (sole member, new member-id)

note over A, B
  Not a claimed instant, zero-overlap guarantee.
  A's in-flight eachMessage (if any) may finish
  after B has already joined. The bounded overlap
  is absorbed downstream by deterministic alert_id
  + idempotent persistence, same backstop used
  everywhere else in Sentinel — not eliminated here.
end note

@enduml
